# Keep the frozen source assets byte-exact.
#
# P0 (progress.md §18.9 item 4) froze SHA-256 over the URDF/STL sources. A
# checkout that rewrites line endings changes those bytes without changing the
# model, which made `tests/test_audit.py::test_source_hashes_unchanged` fail on
# Windows even though nothing had been edited. `-text` disables the conversion
# in both directions, so the hash in `model_parameters.json` keeps its meaning.
#
# Note: this directory is not a git repository yet in this workspace, so the
# attributes take effect when one is initialised and the files are checked out
# again. The current checkout was verified byte-identical by hashing directly.

# CAD / mesh sources
solidwork_graph/**                -text
ref_document/fifty_mujoco/assets/** -text
ref_document/chassis_ref_new/**   -text
ref_document/chassis_ref_origin/** -text
ref_document/chassis_of_hero/**   -text
ref_document/fudan_rl_wheel_leg-main/** -text
ref_document/mjlab_upkie-main/**  -text
ref_document/KYU_Balancing_2026/** -text
ref_document/XYEGA_RM2026_WheelLeg_Infatry_RLdeploy-main/** -text

# by extension, wherever they live
*.STEP -text
*.step -text
*.stp  -text
*.STL  -text
*.stl  -text
*.dae  -text
*.obj  -text
*.urdf -text
*.srdf -text
*.sdf  -text
*.png  -text
*.jpg  -text
*.mp4  -text
*.onnx -text
*.pt   -text

# The generated reports are evidence: normalise them so a diff means a change.
ref_document/fifty_mujoco/reports/** text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
